Driven by a culture of innovation and an ability to adapt quickly, we make every project a unique opportunity to precisely meet our clients' expectations.

Joining Bitumar means becoming part of a committed, collaborative team focused on excellence, in a stimulating environment where your development truly matters.

Reporting to the Corporate Director of Environment, Health, and Safety, the Senior EHS Advisor works collaboratively to implement the organization's health and safety programs to ensure a safe and healthy work environment for all. The Advisor ensures that Bitumar's plants in Quebec comply with applicable laws and regulations. They also collaborate with various stakeholders to promote a workplace health and safety culture focused on prevention.

**Main Responsibilities**

* Support the development and implementation of the EHS strategy;
* Act as a health and safety advisor for all company employees;
* Participate in the development and implementation of best practices in health, safety, and environmental management;
* Stay updated on regulations applicable to our industry at our Quebec sites to ensure compliance;
* Maintain an up-to-date training program on health, safety, and emergency measures to ensure skills are maintained and regulations are met. For certain training sessions, act as the trainer;
* Participate in various committees, including health and safety committees;
* Conduct safety inspections at facilities to ensure compliance with health and safety procedures, guarantee adherence to recommendations, and verify the safe performance of work;
* Assist and advise plant managers in managing major emergency interventions and lead necessary investigations and analyses;
* Monitor and support the execution of the annual EHS Action Plan;
* Be responsible for managing EHS documentation, including program design, EHS data, training documentation, and KPI reports;
* Act as a coach for the site management team to implement transformational changes.

**Desired Profile**

* Proven experience in manufacturing or industrial environments with a solid understanding of CNESST standards, environmental regulations, and workers' compensation laws;
* University education in Health and Safety or a related field;
* Knowledge of occupational health principles and environmental management systems (EHS);
* Excellent writing skills combined with analytical skills for root cause analysis;
* Strong training and development capabilities to educate staff on safety protocols;
* Ability to conduct thorough investigations into incidents or hazards using root cause analysis techniques;
* Effective communication skills to collaborate across departments and promote safety initiatives.

**What We Offer**

* A proactive and people-oriented team;
* A transforming environment conducive to HR innovation;
* Competitive salary based on experience;
* Annual bonus based on individual and company performance;
* Group RRSP with a 6% employer contribution;
* Group insurance with 80% employer contribution;
* $1,000 health care spending account;
* Employee and family assistance program;
* Telemedicine services;
* On-site gym;
* Provided parking, including electric charging stations;
* Free coffee and snacks;
* Recognition program;
* Social activities;
* Remote work options.

